---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import { historyEras, historyMoments } from "../../data/history";
import "../../styles/history.css";
const everyday = [
  { id:"lenses",label:"Snapchat Lenses",type:"CAMERA + COMPUTER VISION",date:"SINCE 2015",
    title:"Those playful face effects? There's some serious technology underneath.",
    intro:"When a puppy nose follows your face or a cartoon mask moves when you smile, the camera has to work out where your eyes, nose, and mouth are. Face-tracking technology makes the effect stay in place.",
    how:"Snap's lenses use camera-based feature tracking, and some Lenses use machine learning. The digital puppy ears themselves are augmented reality artwork, not necessarily generative AI.",
    takeaway:"You were interacting with computer vision years before you thought about AI chatbots.",
    source:"https://help.snapchat.com/hc/en-us/articles/7012366118676-How-Snap-Uses-Information-from-the-Camera",sourceLabel:"Snap · How camera information is used",mark:"⌁"},
  { id:"mail",label:"Email spam filters",type:"PATTERN RECOGNITION",date:"ML-ASSISTED BY 2014",
    title:"The junk mail you never had to open.",
    intro:"Your email provider tries to spot suspicious messages before they reach your inbox. It looks for patterns that are common in spam, while also using other signals.",
    how:"Gmail described adding machine learning to its existing rule-based filtering in 2014. That helped it spot changing spam patterns without needing someone to write every rule by hand.",
    takeaway:"Sometimes the most useful AI is the part you don't notice.",
    source:"https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/workspace/how-machine-learning-g-suite-makes-people-more-productive/",sourceLabel:"Google · Machine learning in Gmail",mark:"✳"},
  { id:"recommendations",label:"What to watch next",type:"PERSONALIZATION",date:"LONG BEFORE CHATBOTS",
    title:"How does Netflix guess what you might enjoy?",
    intro:"Streaming services suggest movies and shows by looking at what you've watched, what you've liked, and patterns across similar viewers.",
    how:"Netflix says its recommendation system uses viewing behavior, title information, and patterns among members. Recommendations are estimates, not a guarantee you'll enjoy something.",
    takeaway:"AI doesn't have to talk to you to influence the choices you see.",
    source:"https://help.netflix.com/en/node/100639",sourceLabel:"Netflix · How recommendations work",mark:"▷"},
  { id:"navigation",label:"Traffic predictions",type:"PREDICTION",date:"IN EVERYDAY ROUTES",
    title:"Your map was predicting the future, a few minutes at a time.",
    intro:"A navigation app doesn't just show where traffic is slow right now. It can also estimate where congestion may build while you're on the road.",
    how:"Google has explained how Maps combines live traffic with historical road patterns and machine learning to predict travel conditions.",
    takeaway:"AI often makes small predictions rather than dramatic announcements.",
    source:"https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/maps/google-maps-101-how-ai-helps-predict-traffic-and-determine-routes/",sourceLabel:"Google · How Maps predicts traffic",mark:"↝"}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="History of AI" description="The history of artificial intelligence, from early ideas to everyday technology you may already use." bodyClass="exhibit-body">
  <SiteHeader subtle />
  <main id="content" class="history-world" data-history-root>
    <section class="hi-hero" aria-labelledby="hi-title">
      <div class="hi-hero__stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hi-hero__inner">
        <div class="hi-hero__copy">
          <a class="hi-back" href="/discover/">← All perspectives</a>
          <p class="hi-eyebrow"><span class="hi-eyebrow__star">✦</span> HISTORY <span class="hi-eyebrow__line"></span> THE LONG STORY</p>
          <h1 id="hi-title">AI didn't begin<br />with <em>ChatGPT.</em></h1>
          <p class="hi-hero__lead">People have been trying to make machines learn, reason, and communicate for generations. Some ideas changed the world. Others took decades to work. Come see how we got here.</p>
          <div class="hi-hero__actions"><a class="hi-action hi-action--main" href="#time-machine">Travel through the eras <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><a class="hi-action hi-action--secondary" href="#everyday-ai">Find the AI you already know ↓</a></div>
          <p class="hi-hero__micro">A selected journey from 1943 to today · Based on historical sources</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hi-clock" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="hi-clock__dial hi-clock__dial--outer"></div>
          <div class="hi-clock__dial hi-clock__dial--mid"></div>
          <div class="hi-clock__dial hi-clock__dial--core"></div>
          <div class="hi-clock__hand"></div>
          <div class="hi-clock__center"><span>AI</span></div>
          <span class="hi-clock__year hi-clock__year--a">1956</span>
          <span class="hi-clock__year hi-clock__year--b">1997</span>
          <span class="hi-clock__year hi-clock__year--c">2017</span>
          <span class="hi-clock__year hi-clock__year--d">2022</span>
          <span class="hi-clock__label">TIME / IDEAS / CHANGE</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hi-thought" aria-labelledby="hi-thought-title">
      <p class="hi-eyebrow hi-eyebrow--muted">BEFORE THE TIMELINE</p>
      <div class="hi-thought__layout"><h2 id="hi-thought-title">AI is older than most people think.</h2><p>Artificial intelligence didn't appear overnight. The field has moved through hopeful beginnings, frustrating setbacks, specialized breakthroughs, and systems that eventually reached our phones. Here's the story in seven chapters.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section id="time-machine" class="hi-eras" aria-labelledby="hi-eras-title">
      <div class="hi-section-top"><div><p class="hi-eyebrow hi-eyebrow--muted">THE TIME MACHINE <span class="hi-eyebrow__line"></span> SEVEN CHAPTERS</p><h2 id="hi-eras-title">Follow the long arc.</h2></div><p>Pick an era to see what people hoped for, what they built, and what we learned along the way.</p></div>
      <div class="hi-era-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Choose a period in AI history">
        {historyEras.map((era,i)=><button type="button" class="hi-era-tab" data-hi-era={era.id} aria-pressed={i===0?"true":"false"} aria-controls={"hi-era-"+era.id}><span class="hi-era-tab__num">{era.index}</span><span class="hi-era-tab__date">{era.years}</span><span class="hi-era-tab__label">{era.label}</span></button>)}
      </div>
      <div class="hi-era-stage" data-hi-era-stage>
        {historyEras.map((era,i)=><article id={"hi-era-"+era.id} class="hi-era-panel" data-hi-era-panel={era.id} aria-labelledby={"hi-era-title-"+era.id} tabindex="-1" hidden={i>0}>
          <div class="hi-era-panel__main">
            <p class="hi-era-panel__index">CHAPTER {era.index} / {era.years}</p>
            <h3 id={"hi-era-title-"+era.id}>{era.title}</h3>
            <p class="hi-era-panel__summary">{era.subtitle}</p>
            <div class={"hi-era-illustration hi-era-illustration--"+era.visual} aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="hi-era-illustration__orbit hi-era-illustration__orbit--a"></span><span class="hi-era-illustration__orbit hi-era-illustration__orbit--b"></span>
              <span class="hi-era-illustration__center">{era.visual==="neuron"?"✳":era.visual==="punch"?"1956":era.visual==="terminal"?">_":era.visual==="winter"?"◇":era.visual==="chess"?"♞":era.visual==="network"?"✧":"AI"}</span>
              <span class="hi-era-illustration__node hi-era-illustration__node--a"></span><span class="hi-era-illustration__node hi-era-illustration__node--b"></span><span class="hi-era-illustration__node hi-era-illustration__node--c"></span>
              <span class="hi-era-illustration__caption">A conceptual illustration, not historical footage</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hi-era-panel__side">
            <div class="hi-era-panel__statement"><span>THE BIG IDEA</span><p>{era.imagined}</p></div>
            <div class="hi-era-panel__statement"><span>WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED</span><p>{era.actual}</p></div>
            <div class="hi-era-panel__lesson"><span>WHAT THIS TEACHES US</span><p>{era.lesson}</p></div>
          </div>
        </article>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hi-milestones" aria-labelledby="hi-milestones-title">
      <div class="hi-section-top"><div><p class="hi-eyebrow hi-eyebrow--muted">THE ACTUAL RECORD</p><h2 id="hi-milestones-title">Twelve moments that shaped AI.</h2></div><p>History is bigger than any timeline. These milestones are starting points, with links to original papers and historical archives.</p></div>
      <div class="hi-milestones__list">
        {historyMoments.map((moment,i)=><details class="hi-milestone" open={i===0}>
          <summary><span class="hi-milestone__year">{moment.year}</span><span class="hi-milestone__title">{moment.title}</span><span class="hi-milestone__expander" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <div class="hi-milestone__body"><p>{moment.description}</p><div><h3>Why it mattered</h3><p>{moment.significance}</p></div><div><h3>Keep it in perspective</h3><p>{moment.correction}</p></div><a href={moment.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{moment.sourceLabel} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </details>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="everyday-ai" class="hi-everyday" aria-labelledby="hi-everyday-title">
      <div class="hi-everyday__intro">
        <p class="hi-eyebrow">YOU WERE THERE, EVEN IF YOU DIDN'T KNOW IT</p>
        <h2 id="hi-everyday-title">You've probably been using AI for years.</h2>
        <p>When people hear “AI,” they often picture a chatbot. But pieces of this technology became part of everyday apps long before you could ask a computer to write an email.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hi-everyday__controls" role="group" aria-label="Choose an everyday AI example">
        {everyday.map((item,i)=><button type="button" class="hi-everyday__tab" data-hi-everyday={item.id} aria-controls={"hi-everyday-"+item.id} aria-pressed={i===0?"true":"false"}><span aria-hidden="true" class="hi-everyday__tabmark">{item.mark}</span><span>{item.label}</span></button>)}
      </div>
      <div class="hi-everyday__stage" data-hi-everyday-stage>
        {everyday.map((item,i)=><article class="hi-everyday__panel" id={"hi-everyday-"+item.id} data-hi-everyday-panel={item.id} tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby={"hi-everyday-title-"+item.id} hidden={i>0}>
          <div class="hi-everyday__art">
            <div class={"hi-everyday__device hi-everyday__device--"+item.id} aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="hi-everyday__devicebar"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
              {item.id==="lenses" ? <div class="hi-face"><div class="hi-face__ears"><i></i><i></i></div><div class="hi-face__head"><b class="hi-face__eye hi-face__eye--left"></b><b class="hi-face__eye hi-face__eye--right"></b><b class="hi-face__nose"></b><b class="hi-face__mouth"></b></div><span class="hi-face__tag">FACE TRACKING</span></div> :
              item.id==="mail" ? <div class="hi-mail"><span>INBOX</span><div>✓ &nbsp; Message from a friend</div><div>✓ &nbsp; Your travel receipt</div><div class="hi-mail__filtered">✦ &nbsp; Suspicious message filtered</div></div> :
              item.id==="recommendations" ? <div class="hi-recs"><span>FOR YOU</span><div class="hi-recs__posters"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="hi-recs__bars"><b></b><b></b><b></b></div></div> :
              <div class="hi-map"><div class="hi-map__roads"></div><svg viewBox="0 0 220 250" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 219Q88 211 66 158T167 85Q196 69 208 26" fill="none" stroke="#d6acff" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="15" cy="219" r="10" fill="#86e4e7"/><circle cx="208" cy="26" r="10" fill="#86e4e7"/></svg><span>ETA 18 MIN</span></div>}
            </div><span class="hi-everyday__art-label">Simplified concept, not an actual app screenshot</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hi-everyday__story">
            <p class="hi-everyday__meta">{item.type} / {item.date}</p>
            <h3 id={"hi-everyday-title-"+item.id}>{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="hi-everyday__lead">{item.intro}</p>
            <div class="hi-everyday__how"><h4>What's happening behind the scenes?</h4><p>{item.how}</p></div>
            <p class="hi-everyday__takeaway">{item.takeaway}</p>
            <a href={item.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{item.sourceLabel} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>)}
      </div>
      <p class="hi-everyday__disclaimer">An important distinction: not every algorithm, animation, or camera filter is AI. Some use fixed rules, while others use computer vision or models that learn from data. Even within the same app, features can work in very different ways.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="hi-perspective" aria-labelledby="hi-perspective-title"><div class="hi-perspective__ring" aria-hidden="true"></div><div><p class="hi-eyebrow hi-eyebrow--muted">THE BIGGER PICTURE</p><h2 id="hi-perspective-title">The future has a history.</h2><p>Every breakthrough was built on earlier ideas, experiments, and mistakes. That's why today's AI is easier to understand when we know where it came from. And it's why we should be curious about what comes next without assuming every prediction will come true.</p></div></section>

    <section class="hi-eli5" aria-labelledby="hi-eli5-title"><div class="hi-eli5__inner"><p class="hi-eyebrow hi-eyebrow--muted">THE EASY VERSION</p>
      <h2 class="hi-eli5__title" id="hi-eli5-title"><span class="hi-eli5__word hi-eli5__word--pink">Explain</span> <span class="hi-eli5__word hi-eli5__word--blue">Like</span> <span class="hi-eli5__word hi-eli5__word--gold">I'm</span> <span class="hi-eli5__word hi-eli5__word--mint">Five:<svg viewBox="0 0 153 22" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" class="hi-eli5__scribble" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M4 10Q37 4 78 8T149 7"/><path d="M11 18Q52 13 87 17T145 15"/></svg></span></h2>
      <p class="hi-eli5__lead">Four ideas, without the complicated words.</p>
      <div class="hi-eli5__cards">
        <article><span>01 / A BIG QUESTION</span><h3>People wanted machines to learn.</h3><p>Scientists started asking if computers could solve problems in ways that seemed smart.</p></article>
        <article><span>02 / SMALL STEPS</span><h3>It took a very long time.</h3><p>There were exciting discoveries and a lot of times when things didn't work yet.</p></article>
        <article><span>03 / EVERYDAY AI</span><h3>AI was already around you.</h3><p>Some camera effects, spam filters, and map predictions used AI before chatbots were popular.</p></article>
        <article><span>04 / WHAT'S NEXT</span><h3>Today's tools are another chapter.</h3><p>AI can do more than it used to, but we still need to check what it gets right and wrong.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <footer class="hi-footer"><span>AI IN PERSPECTIVE · HISTORY IS A SELECTIVE OVERVIEW</span><a href="/methodology">How we use evidence ↗</a><a href="/discover/">← All perspectives</a></footer>
  </main>
  <script>import "../../scripts/history.js";</script>
</BaseLayout>
